namespace ArgentSea;
public sealed class InvalidShardKeyMetadataException : ApplicationException {
  InvalidShardKeyMetadataException();               // "The metadata embedded in the serialized shardkey data does not match the presecribed data types required by the current shardkey definition. The data is corrupt."
  InvalidShardKeyMetadataException(string message);
  InvalidShardKeyMetadataException(string message, Exception innerException);
  InvalidShardKeyMetadataException(Type expected);  // "The metadata embedded in the serialized shardkey does not match the prescribed data type of {expected} required by the current shardkey definition. The data is corrupt."
}
// Carries no properties beyond the message; the Type constructor only interpolates the expected key-part type into the message.
// Raised while turning serialized bytes (or their external string form) back into a ShardKey / ShardChild / ShardGrandChild / ShardGreatGrandChild, or a GhostShardKey, when the embedded type metadata is too short or does not match the key-part types of the target key: the parameterless form for a length/shape failure, the Type form naming the expected key-part type for a position mismatch.
// Callers should treat it as invalid input, not a transient fault: the serialized key was produced for a different key shape or was altered/truncated in transit, so retrying cannot succeed. Code that accepts external key strings (URLs, client payloads) should catch it and report a bad request rather than a server error.
